-- 0024_seed_official_pyq_2015_2016.sql
--
-- The last two papers: RAS 2015 and RAS 2016.
--
-- I said earlier that RPSC only archives answer keys back to 2018. That was
-- wrong, and the mistake was mine: I filtered their exam dropdown on
-- "STATE AND SUB" and the older papers are filed under a different name --
-- "RAS/RTS COMB. COMP. EXAM". Both keys were there the whole time.
--
--   2016  Final Answer Key, released 16/09/2016. RPSC's own link now 404s;
--         the file was recovered from the Internet Archive's copy of that
--         exact URL. Same document, not a third-party transcription.
--   2015  "Revised Answer Key of RAS/RTS Comb.Comp.(Pre) Exam 2013", released
--         18/02/2016. There was no RAS 2015 exam: 2015 was the re-exam of the
--         2013 paper, which is why its key is filed under 2013 and why the
--         revision is dated after the re-exam.
--
-- Alignment was checked against questions answerable without the key before
-- loading either. 2015: Part IX covers Panchayats, O-negative is the emergency
-- donor, the 2015 World Population Day theme, Vigraharaja IV on the Delhi
-- Shivalik pillar -- and Q60 dates itself "as of September 11, 2015". 2016:
-- only a Vidhan Parishad can be abolished, Madhyamika appears in both the
-- Mahabharata and the Mahabhashya, Gulabi Gangaur is Nathdwara's.
--
-- Stems carry their line breaks from the start, unlike 0014/0015 which needed
-- 0020 to put them back.

on conflict do nothing;
